{"kind":"request","text":"Hugh, 2026-10-12 16:15 Eastern: design a journal archive in Git, so that a scope's history can be verified from a clone, separately from the service. Amend notes/2026-10-09-shared-language-volatile-acts.md with the design and get it reviewed.\n\nDecided by Hugh in conversation:\n1. Build the archive (history bytes in Git, with a stated lag), not the acknowledgement barrier. A read states archivedThrough; a client that wants the stronger guarantee waits for its receipt's position to be archived. The \"required custody\" barrier stays unsupported.\n2. Token path: archive pushes use a deployment-level credential, and archive progress is bookkeeping outside history, so archiving creates no entries.\n3. Scopes archived first: lanes, membership, rules and destination. Inboxes are left out. The register is shared across rooms and is not archived to a room's repository.\n4. Detached texts: the archive holds the digest only. Replay from the archive reports those entries as incomplete.\n\nDesign only. No runtime change, no implementation commission.","body":{"conditions":"The amended note states the archive's layout, writer, credential, scope selection, treatment of detached texts, what a clone proves and does not prove, the verifier's Git source, and a sliced implementation plan with witnesses; the checker approves the exact head.","target":"inherit","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}